Z||000000||Hock||05-06-2000||10:57 PM||||I WANT YOU ALL TO KNOW THAT SINCE I'VE BEEN BACK YOU ALL HAVE GIVEN ME THE "FIERO BUG" BACK. JUST LOOKING AT ALL OF THOSE BEAUTIFUL BLACK FIEROS MAKES ME WANT TO GET MINE BACK ON THE ROAD. <P>BUT THAT LEADS TO MY PROBLEM. WHEN I FIRST BOUGHT THE CAR 3 YEARS AGO I WAS IN LOVE WITH IT. THE T-TOPS, THE 5 SPEED, THE BEAUTIFUL SHINE OF THE BLACK PAINT. WELL THEN REALITY BIT ME IN THE FACE. I WENT OVER KILL ON THE ENGINE AND I FOUND OUT I HAD I BENT FRAME. FROM NO FAULT OF MY OWN. ONE OF THE LAST OWNERS WRECKED IT THEN THEY REPLACED THE WHOLE DRIVERS SIDE. THE SAD THING IS THEY DIDN'T TAKE THE TIME TO STAIGHTEN THE FRAME. <P>SO THAT LEADS ME TO MY QUESTION. WHAT SHOULD I DO? ANY SUGGESTIONS???????? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||05-06-2000||11:06 PM||||Check with a local alignment shop and see who they like to see bring their frame repairs in for alignments. A lot of body shops do frame repairs, but not as many do it "right". The alignment guy will know who is good and who is not.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hock||05-06-2000||11:14 PM||||THANKS FOR THE ADVISE. I'LL HAVE TO DO THAT WHEN I GET BACK TO THE STATES!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sillhouette.com||05-07-2000||02:11 AM||||You know it'll probably be easier and better if you get a shell out of the wrecker for a couple of bucks and swap your stuff into it.  You'll also be able to see the complete body of your car before you use it.  I've even heard of people sand blasting it and than having it galvanized.<P>Later||||reg||1
